[about]
Title=06 - Find, Order and Select
Intro=Reaching a record by typing and by Keywords; ordering the list and narrowing it with Filter Records; choosing which fields a row speaks.
Setup=JobTrail is open on the jobs table.
Homework=Find a record three ways, then change the sort and the columns and listen to the difference.

[step]

Say=The quickest way is typing. The first letters of an employer go there.
Key=exa
Hear=Example Widgets Company (sample employer) Accessibility Analyst interviewing, 2 of 4

[step]

Say=Control plus J, Jump to Record -- J for Jump. It searches the field I am on.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump to Match (column, employer) dialog
Hear=Text combo box, blank, ALT+T

[step]

Say=Enter takes me to the record it found.
Key=Enter
Hear=Illustration City Library (fictional) Digital Services Assistant lead, 3 of 4

[step]

Say=Control plus K, Keywords -- K for Keywords. It searches every field, notes included, which is why it is not called Find.
Key=Control+K
Hear=Keywords dialog
Hear=Text combo box, blank, ALT+T

[step]

Say=Enter again, and this is the second match.
Key=Enter
Hear=Sample Health Network (illustration only) Records Coordinator applied, 4 of 4
Note=F3 searches again. Shift reverses: Shift plus F3 searches back, Control plus Shift plus F finds backwards.

[step]

Say=Shift plus K, Say Keywords, reminds me what I looked for.
Key=Shift+F
Hear=find, screen reader

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, Order -- O for Order. Control plus O is Open everywhere, so Order takes Alt.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Hear=Column to sort by list box, employer, 4 of 16, ALT+C

[step]

Say=Typing S jumps to the first field starting with it. That is S, Sierra.
Key=s
Hear=status, 13 of 16

[step]

Say=Enter sorts the list, and the reader reads the row I land on.
Key=Enter
Hear=Records list view
Hear=Sample Health Network (illustration only) Records Coordinator applied, 1 of 4
Note=Shift plus O, Say Order, says it later.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, Filter Records -- F for Filter. It decides which rows I hear, and it writes the condition for me: one box per field, and a symbol in front of a value to compare instead of match.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Hear=Filter combo box, blank, ALT+F

[step]

Say=I want what is still moving: status not rejected.
Key=Enter
Hear=Records list view
Hear=Example Widgets Company (sample employer) Accessibility Analyst interviewing, 1 of 3
Note=Shift plus F, Say Filter, and Shift plus Y, Say Yield -- how many rows it left.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus F clears it. Adding Shift reverses.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=Records list view
Hear=Demo Data Cooperative (made up) Data Quality Specialist rejected, 1 of 4

[step]

Say=Shift plus S, Say Select, names the fields each row speaks.
Key=Shift+S
Hear=select, employer, title, status

[step]

Say=Alt plus S, Select Columns -- Control plus S saves, so Select takes Alt.
Key=Alt+S
Hear=Select Columns dialog
Hear=Columns check list box, employer check box checked, 1 of 16, ALT+C

[step]

Say=I add the date I applied. Space ticks it.
Key=Space
Hear=applied underscore date check box checked, 11 of 16

[step]

Say=Enter applies the choice, and the row is shorter from here on.
Key=Enter
Hear=Records list view
Hear=Example Widgets Company (sample employer) Accessibility Analyst interviewing 2026-09-02, 2 of 4
Note=Three or four fields is the useful range. Every row is heard, so every field costs time.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus J.
Key=
Hear=Jump to Record

[step]

Say=Control plus K.
Key=
Hear=Keywords

[step]

Say=Shift plus F.
Key=
Hear=Say Filter

[step]

Say=Alt plus O.
Key=
Hear=Order Records
